<div class="bt">Likutay Halachos — Orach Chaim, Volume 2</div>
<div class="ht">Hilchos Birchas HaPairos — Halachah 4<br>Part 3 (§§ 12–16) — FINAL<br><span style="font-size:.95rem;font-weight:400">COMPLETE · Based on <span class="lr">LM II:71</span></span></div>

<div class="sn">§ 12 — Pharaoh's Dream: Store the Good Years to Survive the Bad</div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"And it was at the end of two years, and Pharaoh dreamed."</span> This happened on <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> — when Yosef left prison. The miracle came through sleep and its awakening — <span class="v">"and Pharaoh awoke"</span> — derived from the root of supernal <span class="h">Malchus</span> built on <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> through sleep and its awakening, as known in the <span class="h">kavanos</span>.</div>

<div class="p">Pharaoh's dream — seven years of plenty, seven years of famine. The seven bad years swallowed the good: <span class="v">"it was not known that they came into their belly, and their appearance was as bad as at first."</span> All this alludes to the above. Pharaoh saw the source of Israel's exile. The essential exile is from <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> — where our life and length of days are, where the pleasant <span class="h">mochin</span> flow, the <span class="h">no'am</span>, the essential vitality: <span class="v">"wisdom gives life."</span> Therefore exile was in Egypt — the opposite of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>/<span class="h">no'am</span>.</div>

<div class="p">He saw seven good cows — the seven years of plenty — <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> holiness, source of blessing. All from the <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> <span class="h">mochin</span>/<span class="h">no'am</span>. But immediately after the <span class="h">no'am</span> — <span class="v">"seven other cows came up... evil of appearance... I have not seen their like in all Egypt for ugliness"</span> — the absolute evil, the seven famine years, the evil in the <span class="h">chovlim</span> that destroy everything. Immediately when the <span class="h">no'am</span> flows, the <span class="h">chovlim</span> come for rectification. When the evil grips them too strongly, they overpower the <span class="h">ne'imim</span> and damage even <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael's</span> <span class="h">mochin</span> — the seven good years swallowed and forgotten by the seven bad years. From here the essential Egypt exile and all exiles — all from blemished <span class="h">da'as</span>. Adam ate from the Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil — <span class="h">machlokes</span>/<span class="h">chovlim</span> — and was expelled from Gan Eden/<span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>. The exile began through selling Yosef/<span class="h">no'am</span> through <span class="h">machlokes</span>.</div>

<div class="p">The exile lengthens because each time a great <span class="h">tzadik</span> draws the <span class="h">No'am Ha'Elyon</span>/<span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> <span class="h">mochin</span>, the <span class="h">chovlim</span> come for rectification — and when the time hasn't come, they damage the <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> <span class="h">mochin</span> even more. Egypt's exile first began when Avraham said <span class="v">"how shall I know that I will inherit it"</span> — doubting <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael's</span> inheritance. This is <span class="h">chovlim</span> = <span class="h">machlokes</span> and doubts. As soon as Hashem promised him <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, the <span class="h">No'am Ha'Elyon</span> was drawn upon him — but the <span class="h">chovlim</span> immediately came and blemished even the <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> <span class="h">mochin</span> he had attained, until doubts fell into his heart.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore the decree: <span class="v">"know well [yado'a taida] that your seed will be strangers"</span> — <span class="v">"know well"</span> specifically — for the blemish of <span class="h">da'as</span>, the <span class="h">chovlim</span>/<span class="h">chutz la'Aretz</span> <span class="h">mochin</span>. This is Pharaoh's dream: the seven famine years/<span class="h">chovlim</span> swallowed the seven good years/<span class="h">no'am</span>, <span class="v">"unknown that they entered"</span> — the <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> <span class="h">mochin</span> are no longer recognizable, as if they were never drawn.</div>

<div class="p">This applies to every person in every era. Sometimes one is aroused toward holiness, the heart aflame with wondrous yearning. It seems certain one will remain devoted. Then an hour later one falls from one's desire, the heart becomes dulled, the mind confused — completely forgetting the first yearning, as if one never had desire for Hashem's service at all. Sometimes the yearning lasts a long time — yet one still falls and forgets everything.</div>

<div class="p">All holy inspirations come from the <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> <span class="h">mochin</span>/<span class="h">no'am</span>. When they are drawn, the <span class="h">chovlim</span> immediately come — and if one does not rectify them, they damage the <span class="h">no'am</span> <span class="h">mochin</span> and one forgets everything. Therefore one must guard memory carefully — reminding oneself of all first yearnings, all past enthusiasm and <span class="h">kisufin</span> for Hashem. To retain all the <span class="h">reshimos</span> [impressions] of first yearnings in the depths of one's mind — so one can reawaken through them. As Rabbainu writes: one must hold onto the <span class="h">reshimos</span> from earlier days when His light shone upon him.</div>

<div class="p">This is Yosef — the <span class="h">tikkun</span> of Pharaoh's dream. He counseled to preserve the plenty so the land would not be cut off by famine. His counsel: <span class="v">"let them gather all the food of these seven good years, and the food shall be stored"</span> — as soon as any holy good is awakened upon a person, the aspect of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> holiness from which all holiness derives, one should immediately do some holy deed through one's yearning — pray, learn, do a <span class="h">mitzvah</span>. Make storehouses in one's mind to store all the good of the seven good years. A person has free will and power: when holy desire comes, to store and bind it in the depths of the mind, to take this desire in thought and remember it well — never to forget it. Since Yosef the <span class="h">tzadik</span> informs in advance that evil days will come, wanting to make one forget all that good — the wise person understands to store well all the good of the seven good years: to bind the holy desire in thought, and determine that even when the heart becomes dulled by the <span class="h">chovlim's</span> evil, one will strengthen oneself through remembering the first yearning. All the <span class="h">reshimos</span> of earlier yearnings stored in the mind's depths will sustain one's soul in evil days — the seven famine years: <span class="v">"the food shall be stored for the land, for the seven famine years... and the land shall not be cut off by famine."</span></div>

<div class="p">Therefore they are seven and seven — seven good years, seven famine years — corresponding to the Seven Species of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> = the <span class="h">No'am Ha'Elyon</span>, versus the seven nations = the evil in the <span class="h">chovlim</span> = the seven famine years. The essential <span class="h">geulah</span> from Egypt was through Yosef's merit — who withstood temptation and was saved from the love of women. Through this he drew the <span class="h">No'am Ha'Elyon</span>, the root of holy love. Yosef's root is there, in the <span class="h">no'am</span>. Therefore through him the essential <span class="h">geulah</span>: <span class="v">"and Moshe took Yosef's bones with him."</span> Yosef has the power to prevail against the <span class="h">chovlim</span> each time — that the <span class="h">ne'imim</span> rectify the <span class="h">chovlim</span> rather than be damaged by them. This is his merit in interpreting Pharaoh's dream: the famine years do not destroy the plenty years; rather, the plenty sustains through the famine. Therefore: <span class="v">"and you shall bring up my bones from here with you"</span> — to elevate his bones to <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, and through this power to overcome the <span class="h">chovlim</span> until they conquer <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>/<span class="h">no'am</span>/<span class="h">Yosef</span>.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 13 — Visiting <i>Tzadik</i> Graves on <i>Erev Rosh HaShanah</i>; the Ten <i>Tehillim</i></div>

<div class="p">This is why one visits <span class="h">tzadik</span> graves on <span class="h">Erev Rosh HaShanah</span>. The <span class="h">tzadik's</span> passing is into the <span class="h">No'am Ha'Elyon</span> — where all righteous souls ascend: <span class="v">"to gaze upon the pleasantness of Hashem"</span> — <span class="v">"pleasantnesses [ne'amos] at Your right hand forever."</span> At their burial place is the aspect of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>: <span class="v">"the tzadikim shall inherit the land."</span> There the <span class="h">No'am Ha'Elyon</span> flows — <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> holiness, the source of all holiness. All ten levels of holiness are in <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>. Therefore one visits their graves on <span class="h">Erev Rosh HaShanah</span> — to receive <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> holiness there, the <span class="h">No'am Ha'Elyon</span>/<span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> holiness revealed on <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span>.</div>

<div class="p">This is the <span class="h">Tehillim</span> said at <span class="h">tzadik</span> graves — <span class="h">Tehillim</span> are <span class="h">no'am</span>, <span class="v">"ne'im zemiros Yisrael."</span> This is <span class="v">"chavalim naflu li ba'ne'imim"</span> [portions fell to me in pleasantnesses] and <span class="v">"ne'amos biminicha netzach"</span> [pleasantnesses at Your right hand forever] — from the <span class="h">mizmor</span> <span class="v">"Michtam l'Dovid,"</span> the first of the ten <span class="h">Tehillim</span> that Rabbainu established. For the essential <span class="h">tikkun habris</span> — the essential <span class="h">tikkun</span> of all sins — is through the <span class="h">No'am Ha'Elyon</span>, the <span class="h">mochin</span> of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, the essential holiness of <span class="h">da'as</span>. Through the <span class="h">No'am Ha'Elyon</span>, the love of women is broken and one merits the holiness of <span class="h">da'as</span> of <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, the totality of all holiness.</div>

<div class="p">The <span class="h">mizmor</span> begins: <span class="v">"chavalim naflu li ba'ne'imim"</span> — the <span class="h">chovlim</span> fall into the <span class="h">ne'imim</span> for rectification, as Rabbainu explains in the <span class="h">Torah</span>. We still fear the <span class="h">chovlim</span> may overpower the <span class="h">ne'imim</span> and damage them. Therefore it says next: <span class="v">"I will bless Hashem who has counseled me"</span> — Hashem gives counsel through the true <span class="h">tzadik</span> so one can prevail and make the <span class="h">ne'imim</span> overcome the <span class="h">chovlim</span>. <span class="v">"I have set Hashem before me always [tamid]"</span> — <span class="h">tamid</span> is <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>: <span class="v">"the eyes of Hashem are tamid upon it."</span> One must draw <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> holiness upon oneself constantly, never ceasing to yearn. Each time one yearns for <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, the <span class="h">chovlim</span> resist — so one must overcome them each time, <span class="h">tamid</span>. Then Hashem will help one come to <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span> and merit the <span class="h">No'am Ha'Elyon</span> forever — never again falling to the <span class="h">chovlim</span>, but rather rectifying them through the <span class="h">ne'imim</span>: <span class="v">"for You will not abandon my soul to the grave, You will not let Your devout one see destruction"</span> — the <span class="h">chovlim</span> where evil grips. But through the <span class="h">tzadikim's</span> merit, Hashem saves us and we merit <span class="h">No'am Ha'Elyon</span> forever — overcoming the <span class="h">chovlim</span> until they are completely nullified: <span class="v">"ne'amos biminicha netzach."</span> Amain v'amain.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 14 — <i>Shofar</i> = <i>Shufra</i> [Beauty] = <i>No'am</i></div>

<div class="p">Therefore the <span class="h">shofar</span> is called <span class="h">shufra</span> [beauty], as brought — this is the <span class="h">No'am Ha'Elyon</span> awakened through the <span class="h">shofar's</span> sound, the aspect of Yosef who was <span class="v">"beautiful of form."</span> See the entire <span class="h">Torah</span> well from beginning to end — without this one cannot understand our words at all.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 15 — Israel Fruitful in Egypt: <i>No'am</i> Brings Birth and <i>Geulah</i></div>

<div class="p"><span class="v">"And the children of Israel were fruitful and swarmed and multiplied and became very mighty."</span> This was the sprouting of the <span class="h">geulah</span>: <span class="v">"myriads like the plant of the field I made you, and you grew great... your breasts were formed and your hair grew"</span> — ready for <span class="h">geulah</span>. The essential exile is from <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>/<span class="h">no'am</span>. But Hashem had mercy — drawing the <span class="h">No'am Ha'Elyon</span> even in Egypt, from which birth derived. They were fruitful and multiplied greatly — <span class="v">"and the children of Israel were fruitful and swarmed"</span> — and through this came the <span class="h">geulah</span>. The more Israel multiply, the more <span class="h">kavod</span> increases and <span class="h">no'am</span> flows — and the more <span class="h">no'am</span> flows, the more Israel multiply and <span class="h">kavod</span> increases. <span class="v">"And the more they afflicted them, so they multiplied"</span> — the more the exile oppressed (from the <span class="h">chovlim</span>), the more Hashem had mercy and drew the <span class="h">no'am</span>, causing <span class="h">rivui</span> [increase] — the <span class="h">geulah's</span> sprouting. So too in the final <span class="h">geulah</span>: <span class="v">"the small one shall become a thousand, and the young one a mighty nation. I am Hashem — in its time I will hasten it."</span> Through Israel's increase — <span class="h">No'am Ha'Elyon</span> — the <span class="h">geulah</span> will come, speedily in our days, Amain.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 16 — "<i>She'ta'alainu B'Simchah L'Artzainu</i>"</div>

<div class="p">Therefore we pray: <span class="v">"may it be Your will that You bring us up in joy to our land."</span> It is impossible to come to <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, to nullify the obstacles/<span class="h">chovlim</span> and reach <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>/<span class="h">no'am</span>, except through <span class="h">simchah</span> — the aspect of the ten kinds of melody, as Rabbainu writes elsewhere. Through joy — melody, <span class="v">"ne'im zemiros Yisrael"</span> — <span class="v">"fullness of joy is Your Presence"</span> — one merits to come to <span class="h">Eretz Yisrael</span>, which is <span class="h">No'am Ha'Elyon</span>.</div>

<div class="ts">
<div class="sh">✦ Summary — Birchas HaPairos Halachah 4 ✦</div>
<p style="margin-bottom:.8rem"><strong>Core teaching</strong> (<span class="lr">LM II:71</span>): <em>No'am Ha'Elyon</em> [Supernal Pleasantness] = root of all tastes and loves = <em>mochin</em> of <em>Eretz Yisrael</em> = Yosef. <em>Chovlim</em> [destroyers] = <em>chutz la'Aretz mochin</em> = <em>machlokes</em>. When <em>no'am</em> flows, <em>chovlim</em> come for <em>tikkun</em> but can damage the <em>no'am</em> instead.</p>
<p style="margin-bottom:.8rem"><strong>§§1-3</strong>: All <em>berachos</em> connect pleasure to <em>No'am Ha'Elyon</em>. Fruits of <em>EY</em> take precedence. The true praise of <em>EY</em> is the <em>no'am</em> flowing through its fruits. "To gaze upon the <em>no'am</em> of Hashem" = life's purpose.</p>
<p style="margin-bottom:.8rem"><strong>§§4-5</strong>: All obstacles to <em>EY</em> are only obstacles of the mind. Seven nations = seven <em>chovlim</em> vs seven species = <em>no'am</em>. The <em>meraglim</em> said a thing and its opposite.</p>
<p style="margin-bottom:.8rem"><strong>§§6-8</strong>: Egypt's exile from <em>machlokes</em> with Yosef. Moshe couldn't enter because the <em>chovlim</em> would be too strong. "Little by little." <em>Machlokes</em> = exile; <em>shalom</em> = <em>geulah</em>.</p>
<p style="margin-bottom:.8rem"><strong>§§9-11</strong>: <em>Tzedakah</em> = vessel for <em>no'am</em>. <em>Rosh HaShanah</em>: <em>shofar</em> = melody = <em>no'am</em>; <em>pekidas akaros</em>; ten <em>malchuyos</em>, <em>zichronos</em>, <em>shofaros</em> = ten utterances. Yericho conquered by <em>shofar</em>; <em>kinnor na'im</em> = Kena'an.</p>
<p style="margin-bottom:.8rem"><strong>§§12-16</strong>: Pharaoh's dream: store the good years (holy impressions) to survive the bad (<em>chovlim</em>). Visit graves on <em>Erev RH</em>; ten <em>Tehillim</em> = <em>tikkun habris</em> through <em>no'am</em>. Israel's fruitfulness in Egypt = <em>no'am</em> → <em>geulah</em>. Come to <em>EY</em> through <em>simchah</em>.</p>
</div>

